L["A recipe item's tooltip (pattern, plans, formula...) says where it comes from: which vendor sells it, where and for how much, or what drops it. AME learns this as you and your guild play - from merchants you open and recipes you loot - and shares it over sync. Until someone has seen it, the tooltip shows the game's own source text for recipes your profession window lists but you haven't learned."] = true
L["A recipe's tooltip (pattern, plans, formula...) also shows what it makes at today's market price, and what one craft earns after the reagents and the auction house's cut and deposit - red when it loses money. It prices as the Crafting tab and the profession window do: each reagent bought at market, from a vendor or crafted by a recipe you know, whichever is cheapest, and an item searched in the last hour at its cheapest listing. Only the Crafting tab also counts the reagents you hold."] = true
L["A request also goes out as a whisper, so a crafter without AME still sees it. Handed over and declined ones clear after a week."] = true
