L["Every recipe your characters know, most profit per craft first; Market/day is profit per craft times how many the whole market takes a day - the size of the opportunity, not what you'd earn (that's your share of the sales, after the other sellers'). Click a column to sort by it. Reagents count at the cheapest way to get them - bought at market price, from a vendor, crafted from cheaper materials, or, for what you already hold, at what selling it would net (listing costs the AH cut, buying doesn't). Signal is the product's market signal, as the Market screener shows it. Click a row for the breakdown: how it's made, its reagents, and what it sells for. A recipe that requires a tool (a Salt Shaker, a Blacksmith Hammer) or a place (an anvil, a forge) gets a Tools section: whether one of your characters has the tool, and how to get one - make it (or the pattern that teaches it, with its price and who sells it), buy it from a vendor, or the auction house. (Open the profession window once so AME knows what each recipe requires.) Queue puts one craft on the craft queue, and Reagents to a list puts one craft's reagents on a shopping list."] = true
L["Every scan is kept for 2 days (the 2D chart), a point per hour for 7 days (the 7D chart), a point per day for 60 days, then a point per week for a year. Your ledger keeps 90 days."] = true
