L["With Baganator, AME adds three icon corners and a sort. In Baganator's settings, under Icons, place AME: signal (the item's market signal as its icon: BUY or SELL, and HOLD and WAIT if you ask for them), AME: tip (what to do with it, as the Selling tab's Tip says: Arb, DE or Vend, and Sell if you ask for it) and AME: value (what it's worth, in the coin's colour) in a corner; pick AME: worth as the sort to put the most valuable stacks first. The tip only marks a slot: what's junk is Baganator's own. Settings, General, Other addons says what the tip and value corners show, or turns it all off."] = true
L["With the Market overview switched on (Settings, General), the toolbar's first buttons switch the Market tab between the Screener (this list) and the Overview: indexes and totals for the whole auction house (see Market overview)."] = true
L["With the auction house open, AME's window is the auction house. The tabs stay the same, and each gains what the auction house allows."] = true
L["With the auction house open, Shift-click a row to search for it there. While the search box has focus, Shift-click an item link anywhere to search for it by name."] = true
L["With the game's window: open AME beside it"] = true
L["With v2 (the default), every scan goes to the whole guild at once, and hours you missed in the last week are filled in from whoever has them - a point per hour for the 7D chart, and whole days for days you have nothing of. It's paced at about one message a second, so a full scan takes several minutes to arrive, in the background. If sync seems to slow your game, pick v1 (lighter) under Guild sharing: you still get scans, the original way. Guild sharing shows how many of the week's hours you have."] = true
L["With your profession window open, adds the reagents of the selected recipe - as many times as you'll craft it."] = true
L["Withdraw"] = true
L["Within its usual range"] = true
L["Without Auctionator, the auction house window gets a Shopping tab next to Buy, Sell and Auctions. Pick a list on the left and click Search all: AME searches each item in turn, as fast as the game allows, and shows how many you still need, the cheapest listing, your top price, and what the rest costs. The sidebar shows how many items are still short on each list. Click an item for its listings, cheapest first, with how long each has left (for gear the game often gives only a range, such as 2-12 h); scroll for more. Buy asks the game for the price, then Confirm buys it - the game wants a click for each purchase - or Cancel backs out. Confirm only ever buys the item on screen: picking another item drops a purchase that wasn't confirmed. Clicking an item while Search all runs searches it first, then Search all goes on. The list counts down as you buy. Shift-click an item (in your bags, in chat) to search for it there, and Search the AH on AME's pages searches this tab too."] = true
